      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. Per doc, the command name is VENDOR_CC_GET_BOOT_FLAG. Missed the most recent update.\nBut, still the design doc describes this with two expressions \u0027Flags\u0027 and \u0027Mood\u0027.\nThis is how I understand the design description: There are two kinds boot flags \"NO_BOOT (Bit 1)\" and \"RECOVERY (BIT 0)\". A combination of these two bits is a mode, and there are four kinds of boot_mode.\n\ndnojiri@, would you confirm if my understanding is correct? can we consolidate these expressions?",
